{"ts": "2026-10-26T00:17:57.573320Z", "run_id": "r-20261026T0016Z-eac0", "unit": "openspec:vault-service-identity-fast-check", "seq": 16, "type": "delegate.result", "question": "Q-001", "id": "Q-001", "status": "answered", "reason": "The project's own documents settle this. proposal.md (Impact) says the stack-level check needs Docker, which the gates do not have, so a person runs it after the merge and the gates prove the per-call allocation bound; tasks.md forbids any test needing Docker or a network beyond loopback; the spec's scenarios are all in-process (allocation bounds, loopback gRPC server, TestMain allocation), none at stack level; the compose file confirms the 128m limit the person's check uses. No business or product decision is left open.", "called": true, "tasks": ["1.1", "2.1", "3.1"], "target": null, "kind": "ambiguous", "profile": "delegate-fable", "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "cli": "claude-code", "cost_usd": 1.0639615, "decision": "answer", "answer_sha256": "945e1de5bd0e3c6ffa42d9647b95520475bf9ffc15fef3fb3ef306f283d68626", "checked": [{"ref": "openspec/changes/vault-service-identity-fast-check/proposal.md:56", "quote": "The stack-level check (300 proxied calls at concurrency 16 against the vault at its stock 128m limit with no 5xx and\n  peak RSS under 100 MiB, and 16 parallel callers with wrong tokens for 60 s without a restart) needs Docker, which the\n  gates do not have: a person runs it after the merge. The gates prove the per-call allocation bound it rests on.", "claim": "The proposal already assigns the stack-level acceptance to a person after the merge and says the gates cover only the per-call bound."}, {"ref": "openspec/changes/vault-service-identity-fast-check/tasks.md:8", "quote": "No test may need Docker or a network beyond `127.0.0.1`.", "claim": "The tasks forbid any Docker-based test, so the stack-level check cannot be one of the unit's tests."}, {"ref": "spec:specs/vault-identity-verification/spec.md#scenario-validations-allocate-little", "quote": "**THEN** `runtime.MemStats.TotalAlloc` grew by less than 1 MiB (1048576 bytes) across the thirty calls", "claim": "The spec's acceptance is the in-process allocation bound, not a stack-level run."}, {"ref": "spec:specs/vault-identity-verification/spec.md#scenario-concurrent-calls-share-one-connection", "quote": "**THEN** all sixteen succeed and the listener accepted exactly one connection", "claim": "Concurrency sixteen is checked in-process against a loopback gRPC server, not in Docker."}, {"ref": "infra/compose/docker-compose.yml:166", "quote": "mem_limit: 128m", "claim": "The vault adapter's stock compose limit is 128m, matching the person's check described in the proposal; nothing asks to change it."}]}
